# Files chezmoi should actively delete from the target that are no longer managed.
# chezmoi does not auto-delete a deployed file just because its source entry was
# removed — entries here are the explicit, declarative fix for that gap.

# specstory-cleanup-and-crash-recovery (2026-11-07): sync-memory retired entirely.
# These two global template files were deployed by earlier chezmoi applies and would
# otherwise linger forever as orphaned, unreferenced leftovers on any machine that had
# this skill installed before the removal.
.claude/skills/setup-memory-workflow/scripts/sync-memory.py.template
.claude/skills/setup-memory-workflow/assets/sync-memory-skill.md.template

# claude-profile-mismatch-guard retired (2026-11-17): replaced by the ccenv-profile-guard
# Claude Code mod in the separate zsh-claude-env project. The deployed script would
# otherwise linger on every machine's ~/.local/bin forever, since its source entry alone
# being removed doesn't delete it.
.local/bin/claude-profile-mismatch-guard

# claude-tooling-write-guard retired (2026-11-17): replaced by the chezmoi-tooling-guard
# Claude Code mod in this repo's own chezmoi-personal marketplace (packages.yaml installs
# it machine-wide). Same orphaned-leftover reasoning as the entry above.
.local/bin/claude-tooling-write-guard
